# FROM THE NEWS:
# ---
# Safer upgrade procedure
# =======================
# A safer approach is to add Python 3.14 support to your system first,
# and only then remove Python 3.13.  However, note that this involves two
# rebuilds of all the affected packages, so it will take noticeably
# longer.
#
# First, enable both Python 3.13 and Python 3.14, and then run the upgrade
# commands:
#
#     */* PYTHON_TARGETS: -* python3_13 python3_14
#     */* PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET: -* python3_13
#
# Then switch PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET and run the second batch of upgrades:
#
#     */* PYTHON_TARGETS: -* python3_13 python3_14
#     */* PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET: -* python3_14
#
# Finally, switch to the final version and upgrade:
#
#     */* PYTHON_TARGETS: -* python3_14
#     */* PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET: -* python3_14
#
# You may wish to remove the target overrides after the defaults switch.
# Alternatively, you can keep them to block the next automatic upgrade
# to Python 3.15, and upgrade manually then.

*/* PYTHON_TARGETS: -* python3_14
*/* PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET: -* python3_14
